According to a report by Intel Market Research, Global Acetate Tow (Cellulose Acetate Tow) Market size was valued at USD 3.20 billion in 2025. The market is expected to move from USD 3.10 billion in 2026 to USD 2.00 billion by 2034, exhibiting a compound annual growth rate of –5.3% during the forecast period.
Acetate tow consists of continuous cellulose acetate filaments produced from wood derived pulp or cotton linters through a chemical acetylation process. The fibers display high absorbency, uniform denier and a characteristic crimp that enables reliable filtration performance while remaining biodegradable under industrial composting conditions.
